  "summary": "The code suffered from a critical open redirect vulnerability due to loose regex matching and inefficient per-request compilation. I have refactored the validation logic to use a strict, pre-compiled regex and updated naming conventions to follow PEP 8 standards.",
  "fixed_code": "from flask import Flask, redirect, request\nimport re\nfrom typing import Union\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n# Pre-compile regex for performance and security\n# Enforce https and strict domain anchoring\nALLOWED_DOMAIN_PATTERN = re.compile(r'^https://(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/')\n\n@app.route('/redirect')\ndef redirect_to_target() -> str:\n    '''\n    Get target URL from request, validate against strict pattern,\n    and redirect to the target URL.\n    '''\n    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n    if target and ALLOWED_DOMAIN_PATTERN.match(target):\n        return redirect(target)\n    else:\n        return \"Invalid target\""
